; Runs the repository's Form-native independent AI review panel on the
; corrected meaning-space seed. Answers are persisted by review-ask.fk under
; (ra-run-dir) before this cell returns them.
;
; witnessed: pending independent panel
import "../form/form-stdlib/core.fk"
import "review-panel.fk"
import "review-ask.fk"

(ra-review
  "docs/coherence-substrate/form-neutral-meaning-space-review-seed.md"
  "Review this candidate architecture against the user's stated intent. Be adversarial and independent. Determine whether it makes each meaning—including a higher-dimensional meaning with no local expression—a form-neutral symbol whose recipe uses only other neutral symbols, then maps that meaning into NL and PL surfaces. Check that it imposes no ontology rules, that trust/sovereignty/vitality remain guidance, and that words, Chinese/Japanese characters, symbols, common memes, PL operators/types/code forms, polysemy, context, lexical gaps, frequency, inverse graph queries, and retrainable embeddings are represented honestly. Do not edit any file or propose unrelated product features. Return: VERDICT (PASS or REVISE), the three most important located objections, a corrected minimal schema if revision is needed, and a direct assessment of each of the three examples.")
